# Force LF on the files that the container executes through a shebang.
#
# A Windows checkout with the default `core.autocrlf=true` writes these with
# CRLF. The kernel then reads `#!/bin/bash\r` as an interpreter literally named
# "bash\r", cannot find it, and the machine dies on boot with exit 127 — which
# is what killed the first attempt at #290 on the sibling app. CI builds on
# Linux and never saw it. These rules make the hazard structurally impossible
# regardless of who builds the image or from which platform.
#
# Deliberately NOT `*.js`: those are loaded by node, which handles CRLF fine,
# and a blanket rule would renormalize several files that are committed with
# CRLF today — a large diff with real conflict surface and no boot-safety gain.
*.sh         text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
